---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

// Update this whenever the page below changes. A /now page that has
// clearly gone stale is worse than not having one.
const updated = 'October 6, 2026';
---

<Layout
  title="Now | Joe Fazio"
  description="What Joe Fazio is studying and building at the moment."
>
  <h1>Now</h1>
  <p class="meta">Last updated {updated}</p>

  <p>
    What I am studying and building at the moment.
  </p>

  <h2>Next: CompTIA Security+</h2>

  <p>
    Security+ is an entry-level security certification covering network
    security, threat identification, access control and incident response. It
    is the next certification I plan to study for. My coursework already covered
    the framework side of this: for the <a href="/projects">BRHS risk
    assessment</a>, we weighed NIST CSF 2.0 against CIS Controls v8 and chose the
    one that fit the client. Security+ is the structured
    version of the same material with an exam attached.
  </p>

  <h2>Also next: PowerShell automation</h2>

  <p>
    Scripts that handle real systems administration tasks: parsing log files,
    bulk user operations and scheduled health checks. These are tasks that come
    up in most IT roles. They will go in a public repository as they are
    finished.
  </p>

  <h2>This site</h2>

  <p>
    Built in Astro with Claude Code and deployed through Cloudflare Pages. It is
    the best current example of how I work. Terraform for the
    Cloudflare configuration and a small Cloudflare Worker are the next pieces. <a
    href="/projects">The projects page</a> has the current state of it.
  </p>
</Layout>
